/*
  CarAnimation.strings
  TeslaSync — P4 shared surface · 0190 · CarAnimation (Apple)

  The P1/S10 i18n catalog contribution for this surface. The web `components/motion/CarAnimation.tsx`
  resolves three localized strings of its own — the `role="img"` accessibility labels for the silhouette
  (`carAnimation.tesla` → 'Tesla vehicle illustration'), the charging bolt (`carAnimation.charging` →
  'Charging'), and the wheel loader (`carAnimation.loading` → 'Loading'). The battery gauge has no
  `role`/`aria` in the source, so it owns no key. Those three keys are mirrored below with the exact web
  fallback copy.

  These entries fold into the app `Localizable.xcstrings` master catalog at integration time (which already
  carries `translation.carAnimation.*`); they are kept in a per-surface table ("CarAnimation") so each
  parallel surface prompt owns its own strings. In test / preview bundles `NSLocalizedString` returns the
  value below, keeping the labels deterministic.
*/

/* Accessibility label for the animated Tesla silhouette (web role="img" aria-label). */
"carAnimation.tesla" = "Tesla vehicle illustration";

/* Accessibility label for the animated charging bolt glyph (web role="img" aria-label). */
"carAnimation.charging" = "Charging";

/* Accessibility label for the spinning wheel loader (web role="img" aria-label). */
"carAnimation.loading" = "Loading";
